<title>UK: Exxon and insurers near Valdez deal - sources.</title>
<headline>Exxon and insurers near Valdez deal - sources.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. oil giant Exxon and the international insurance market are close to settling the final part of a payout stemming from the Exxon Valdez oil tanker spill in 1989, industry sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>After several months of negotiations, Exxon and the insurers, among whom the Lloyd's of London reinsurance vehicle Equitas has a one third exposure to the claim, are near to agreeing on a sum thought to be not substantially in excess of the $410 million awarded by a court in Texas last June.</p>
</text>
